      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city’s name comes from the Santa Maria River that flows through the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ohmyfacts.com/world/cities/30-facts-about-santa-maria/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The historic Santa Maria Inn, built in 1917, still stands on South Broadway and is a registered landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Maria%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Santa Maria hosts the Santa Maria Valley Historical Society Museum, which displays over 3,000 photos and artifacts of Chumash, Mission, and Rancho eras.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitcalifornia.com/places-to-visit/santa-maria/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Santa Maria Museum of Flight showcases the region’s aviation history, while the Santa Maria Philharmonic Society brings classical music to life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
